dynrec: generic support for 64-bit, big-endian and strict alignment hosts, and performance improvements

Shared code for the alpha, mips64, sparc64 and PowerPC backends:

- 64-bit big-endian host fixes: core_dynrec.callback is Bit32u as written
  by generated code, lower 32bit of cpu.direction, lflags.type and
  cpu.stack.mask on big-endian hosts
- alignment-safe accessors for the code page write map
- backend hooks: code cache placement (DRC_CACHE_ALLOC), protected_regs
  indexed by host register (DRC_PROTECTED_REGS), padded stanzas only for
  calls that may be replaced, inline TLB memory accesses
  (DRC_USE_INLINE_MEMORY), branch conditions from the guessed last flags
  operation checked against lflags.type at runtime (DRC_USE_INLINE_FLAGS),
  inline push/pop (DRC_USE_INLINE_STACK), the carry into ADC/SBB/RCL/RCR
  (DRC_USE_INLINE_CARRY), and direct continuation at the last target of
  RET and indirect JMP/CALL (DRC_USE_INDIRECT_LINK)
- string operations on runs within a page through the host pointer, and
  as block writes into handler memory (chained VGA in 4 byte groups,
  unchained VGA with one address translation per run)
- RCL/RCR flags-invalidation variants without flag materialization
- string direction taken from cpu.direction, the signed parameter may
  arrive zero-extended from generated code
- backend hooks for link jumps patched to direct jumps (DRC_USE_LINK_PATCH),
  flag-setting ALU operations, shifts and INC/DEC inline in the call stanza
  (DRC_USE_INLINE_FLAGS_OPS, code only needed by the full function is
  skipped once it is replaced), FPU arithmetic (DRC_USE_INLINE_FPU_ARITH)
  and FPU stack, register moves and m32/m64 loads/stores (DRC_USE_INLINE_FPU)
- optional perf map of the generated blocks with DOSBOX_PERF_MAP set
- PAGESIZE config.h template
- shared parts of the PowerPC backends: write map accesses on big-endian
  hosts, little-endian access to guest immediates (gen_add_LE,
  gen_mov_LE_word_to_reg), backend cache block hooks, POWERPC id

Signed-off-by: René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

